messages:
Marta (Docs): Heads-up: found a few stale anchors and an example that assumes tools is always an array on the structured-output page. Opened a small PR to update links + add a resilient parse snippet: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/576
Noah (SDK): Nice. Can you add both TS and Python examples and a tiny helper that normalizes the envelope? Folks keep hitting TypeErrors when tools === null.
Ivy (Eng-ML): Confirmed. Older model runners returned null for empty tool lists. Runtime change coming but we need docs to cover both shapes. Suggest showing schema + runtime-shim.
Marta (Docs): Plan: add a Compatibility subsection with: 1) TS parse shim, 2) Python shim, 3) JSON Schema that accepts array or null, and 4) mention that runtime v2 will return [] soon.
Riley (Eng-Runtime): Correct, v2 will default to [] next week. No rollback planned. Docs should keep the shim until we guarantee all clients upgraded.
Noah (SDK): Suggested TS helper: ```ts
export function normalizeTools(resp: any){
  if (Array.isArray(resp.tools)) return resp.tools;
  if (resp.tools == null) return [];
  return [resp.tools];
}
```
Marta (Docs): Adding that. I'll also include a one-liner unit test in docs/tests/snippets/test_normalize_tools.js to run the snippet with tools=null and ensure no exception.
Ivy (Eng-ML): Also include the schema example: ```json
{"type":"object","properties":{"tools":{"type":["array","null"],"items":{"type":"object"}}},"required":["tools"]}
```
CI-Bot: Preview deployed: https://deploy-preview-576--docs.redwood.ai/structured-output (expires in 48h) :white_check_mark:
Noah (SDK): LGTM once both snippets are in. I'll follow up with an SDK helper PR to match the docs helper.
Marta (Docs): Thanks! I'll merge after CI and add a changelog line mentioning anchor fixes + compatibility guidance.
